      "writtenOn": "2024-11-14T15:48:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this isn\u0027t a handle, this is just a pointer. So use `nullptr` instead. Also are we sure this is even needed here? We do a similar thing in Ganesh, but that was because the validation layers had a bug and still tried to access pBindings even if bindingCount was zero. By the Vulkan spec it should be safe to put any ptr here if bindingCount is zero (i.e. just always do `bindingLayouts.data()`). You should confirm whether or not current validation layers still have this issue. If we still do need this then you should copy over the comment from ganesh,\n```\n// Setting to nullptr fixes an error in the param checker validation layer. Even though\n// bindingCount is 0 (which is valid), it still tries to validate pBindings unless it is\n// null.\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 99,
        "startChar": 58,
        "endLine": 99,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "72294a9dc9e0b733d01c9858be765a0a65ea5aa6",
